How about this:  a scroll of reincarnation (very rare, I would think).

"Your hands look translucent."

On the next hit on a creature (hand to hand only, I would think), you become
that creature.  Could be a lot of fun with ghosts.  You would become a
reincarnated version of the ghost (living, not a ghost) and have any
additional knowledge (yours + theirs, spells, items, etc.) and abilities.
But, you have the same strength (physical attributes) that the character
had.  I think you should probably either keep your experience level or
possibly average it with theirs.  Could be a nice little trap if you happen
to become a ghost who was first level and happened to have wandered down to
level 15 of the dungeon.  Nyuk, nyuk, you lose half your levels.  Also, his
dog (or any tamed monsters) should recognize him and be tame to you now, too.
Your own dog might not recognize you anymore, but then again, it might.


